From: =?UTF-8?q?=E9=AB=98=E5=BA=86=E4=B8=B0?= <gao.qingfeng@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 12:28:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/29] fix(chunk/cache): LRU eviction queue review fixes

Address independent-review findings (PR #26 review):

- evict_lru now pops candidates one at a time (peek-then-pop) instead of
  batch-popping up to 1024 entries: a small eviction no longer discards
  the unprocessed tail of the queue, which previously drained it and
  degraded every subsequent eviction to the full-directory atime scan.
- Re-check the access index after the metadata await and before
  remove_file to close the TOCTOU window where a concurrent load can
  re-access the key.
- evict_lru_fallback builds the indexed-filename set and skips entries
  still owned by the in-memory LRU index (protects hot entries).
- record_access keeps the heap bounded: when it exceeds
  live*16+1024 entries it rebuilds from the access-index snapshot,
  dropping stale entries (prevents unbounded growth for caches that
  never evict).
- Regression tests: 1200-entry queue survives a one-entry eviction;
  200k record_access calls keep the queue bounded; comments clarify
  bytes_used deduction in the lazy test.
- hot_bytes comment now states it is observability-only and must not be
  used for budget decisions.
